label: Soil Component
description: >-
  The dominant soil component of one map unit. SDA can return several
  majcompflag='Yes' rows per mukey; blue-ribbon's pickDominantComponent picks
  highest comppct_r with a cokey tiebreak, and that selection happens BEFORE
  this edge exists.
index: mukey
fields:
  mukey:
    type: utf8
    label: Map Unit Key
    description: SSURGO map unit this component belongs to
    nullable: false
    validations:
      minLength: 1
      maxLength: 30
  cokey:
    type: utf8
    label: Component Key
    description: SSURGO component key -- the handle for the dwelling-rating lookup
    nullable: false
    validations:
      minLength: 1
      maxLength: 30
  compname:
    type: utf8
    label: Series
    description: Soil series name, e.g. "Kalkaska"
    nullable: false
    validations:
      minLength: 1
      maxLength: 100
  comppctR:
    type: uint8
    label: Component Percent
    description: Percent of the map unit this component represents
    nullable: false
    validations:
      min: 0
      max: 100
  drainagecl:
    type: utf8
    label: Drainage Class
    description: >-
      SSURGO drainage class. NULL is data, not absence of data -- a component
      with no drainage class is not dry, and blue-ribbon's isDryComponent
      treats null as not-dry rather than as an error.
    nullable: true
    validations:
      maxLength: 60
  wtdepannmin:
    type: f64
    label: Water Table Depth
    description: >-
      Minimum annual water table depth, cm. NULL means no water table in the
      profile, which is HALF THE DRY TEST -- so here a null is not merely data,
      it is the positive signal. isDryComponent requires wtdepannmin === null.
    nullable: true
    validations:
      min: 0
      max: 1000
